# A command that is random UNLESS you pin its seed. litmus injects a per-run
# seed as the environment variable `LITMUS_SEED`. Here the base seed is fixed
# and never changes across runs (we set runs' derived seed from a constant
# base), and the program uses LITMUS_SEED as its PRNG seed.
#
# Because `seed = 7` is fixed and the derived per-run seed = base + run_index,
# each run gets a DIFFERENT but DETERMINISTIC seed. To make every run identical
